A||||4||GREENDANO||3.2 hesitation
Z||000000||GREENDANO||06-01-99||08:44 PM||||I just restored/rebuilt my 85 GT nose to tail and upgraded the 2.8 to a 3.2.  Question for anyone that might have seen this....I have a WICKED hesitation when you first squeeze into it, It auto BTW.  Fuel pressure is on the money 48 PSI at WOT, actually I've bumped it up a couple pounds at several occasions starting at stock, not much help.  Every sensor is new, EVERY sensor.  I'm not an idiot here, but I feel like it.  If someone has an idea I'll check it.  I have to dig into and get the power that I know I'm missing.<br>  Thanks
Z||000001||Carrolles||06-02-99||06:22 AM||||Write to Ed Parks at the Fiero Factory at:<p>www.fierofactory.com<p>Or call him in Alabama at:<p>(256) 420-5391<p>He has always been very helpful to me and knows these cars inside and out.<p>Good luck,<br>Carroll
Z||000002||Shaun41178||06-03-99||12:49 AM||||Check to make sure that the throttle position sensor is not sticking.  There is a little metal piece that reacts along with the movement of the TPS sensor.  If this has somehow gotten stuck somehow it could give a hesitation when accelerating at idle or other engien rpm.  This happened to my TPS and I had a hesitation when I put the throttle down.  I noticed the TPS sensor was sticking and I fixed it and no more hesitation.  you should not have to buy a new sensor if this is the problem.  Good luck<br>Shaun
Z||000003||GREENDANO||06-03-99||03:58 PM||||My TPS is brand new a year ago.  Plus I checked the TPS sweep with a TECH 1, I also had the  hesitation you had, That's why it's new.<br>  The problem occured after I rebuilt the engine.  It pretty much gets better once the motor is warm.  I'm leaning towards an engine ground.  (Ground heats up and expands, makes a better contact) Only one hole in that theory,  why it only happens under a slight tip-in load and not at anything above about 20% throttle.  If I pin the throttle WOT it goes pretty well.<br>  I'm still working on it, it's tough to do this all day and come home and work on more driveability at home.<br>  Dan-O<br> 
Z||000004||GREENDANO||06-03-99||05:48 PM||||All right, I hang my head in shame, but at least I found it!!!<br>  Guess who forgot to ground A-B in the ALDL?  ME.  I remember dialing in the timing but I never grounded the B terminal before I set the timing.  So my timing was 10 degrees retarded.  So after bumping my timing to 10 then to 12 degrees, WOW.  Now I'm making 200 HP like I was supposed to.  HOLY COW.  Night and day difference.  <br>  So there, put that in your memory banks for  future reference.<br>  Thanks for the input.<br>  Dan-O
